          "semanticAnchorId": "ANCHOR_KEPLER_ORBITS_AREAS",
          "title": "1. Keplers First Law (Orbits) and Second Law (Areas)",
          "contentMarkdown": "Keplers First Law: Planets move in elliptical orbits with the Sun at one focus (closest is perihelion, farthest is aphelion). Keplers Second Law: Areal velocity is constant ($$dA/dt = L/(2m) = \\\\text{const}$$), meaning speed is maximum at perihelion and minimum at aphelion due to angular momentum conservation.",
